      <activity id="0b5dee33-5b67-5226-82df-c28e0a784ece" activityNameId="a7ac4b99-ec24-5c6c-83db-e47b1169bfa1" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Excavation, hydraulic digger (proj. 500)</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Excavation, hydraulic digger (proj. 500)
This module is based on the data included in the report Oekoinventare von Energiesystemen 1996. The diesel consumption and the emissions are updated using the Swiss "Offroad database" and applied to year 2000. This moduleshould not be used if its relative importance would be high in a certain environmental inventory.;
Synonyms: excavator, engine; 
UUID: 4af488fe-42c2-319e-a559-8ddde43b396c
Includes the inputs "hydraulic digger" for infrastructure, lubricating oil and fuel consumption, and some measured air emissions as output.
Location: Certain elementary flows or intermediate product flows are extrapolated from Swiss conditions.
Technology: Average current technology for one typical machine representing the category.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Some data from the LCA study Oekoinventare von Energiesystemen 1996 and emissions from the Swiss "Offroad" database. 
Extrapolations: See geography
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4af488fe-42c2-319e-a559-8ddde43b396c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
